{"agent":"n1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"A fully quoted flag is still a flag in the parsed argv, but the new mask treats any token whose entire spelling is one quote pair as data and `_matches_flag` skips it. Given `git push origin main '--force'` or `git push \"--force\"`, posix tokenization yields the word `--force`, `_quoted_mask` returns true because the retained token is `'--force'`/`\"--force\"` with content equal to that word, and the force push is allowed. Shell parsing strips those quotes, so the command that actually runs is a real `git push` with the force flag — the case this change promised would stay refused. Exempting quote spelling, rather than matching flag words in the parsed argv and ignoring the flag text only when it is a substring of a larger argument, is the wrong predicate.","digest":"9f86df70a3b67afc","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_matches_flag","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_matches_flag"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11807,"diff_sha":"ccc1b43c8ceb37e80d7626849689a0c9a573dead7e15c545f1932aee5404af23","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-hook-flag-match-matches-quoted-text","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":12.3,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"c644a6852faff16f","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-hook-flag-match-matches-quoted-text.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261111T191403Z-453fad32.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"4d90aeb58f00","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"06686721b640a61512e6d1802bcb4844789a588b","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/forbidden.py":"100644 898d47ab4d13cc5763f96ae99910e4047c9a0b0d","tests/test_f